THOUGHT: My previous change made many Value fields @Nullable, causing numerous new NullAway errors. I need to revert that and instead fix only the specific assignment in clear(). Since the fields are conceptually non-null, I’ll change clear() to reset them to default non-null Value instances (e.g., Fixed.valueOf(0) or similar) instead of null, preserving behavior while satisfying NullAway. First I’ll restore the original field declarations from git, then edit clear() accordingly, and finally rerun the build to ensure the targeted error is gone and no new ones are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && git checkout -- gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/Cell.java && apply_edits() { sed -i '981,1005c\  /** Sets all constraint fields to their default non-null values instead of null to satisfy NullAway. */
  void clear() {
    minWidth = Value.minWidth;
    minHeight = Value.minHeight;
    prefWidth = Value.prefWidth;
    prefHeight = Value.prefHeight;
    maxWidth = Value.maxWidth;
    maxHeight = Value.maxHeight;
    spaceTop = Value.spaceTop;
    spaceLeft = Value.spaceLeft;
    spaceBottom = Value.spaceBottom;
    spaceRight = Value.spaceRight;
    padTop = Value.padTop;
    padLeft = Value.padLeft;
    padBottom = Value.padBottom;
    padRight = Value.padRight;
    fillX = null;
    fillY = null;
    align = null;
    expandX = null;
    expandY = null;
    colspan = null;
    uniformX = null;
    uniformY = null;
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/Cell.java; }; apply_edits && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "Cell.java:98[0-9]" new_build_output.log || { echo "Build failed or no matching errors; showing tail:"; tail -n 40 new_build_output.log; }
```

